# P1.5-7: Battery API randomization (navigator.getBattery)
#
# Scope (ONE issue): Override navigator.getBattery() inside addInitScript to
# return a randomized-but-session-stable BatteryManager. Real headful Chrome
# 145 on a desktop often exposes `charging: true, level: 1.0` (AC powered),
# but this precise combo is a bot signal when seen across many sessions.
# Real-user distributions span both charging states and levels 0.3-0.95.
#
# Randomization happens ONCE at addInitScript time (per page load), so both
# the charging state and level are stable within a single session but vary
# across sessions -- this matches real-user behavior where a battery reading
# barely moves during a short browsing session.
#
# Anchor: post-P1.5-6 output of rednoteTools.js. Same stacking pattern --
# inserts a new try/catch before the closing `});` of addInitScript.
#
# Red lines: No fetch/XHR/cookie overrides. No BatteryManager prototype
# modification (only replaces the getBattery() promise). chargingTime /
# dischargingTime are Infinity per MDN typical behavior for a plugged-in
# desktop or fully-known battery.
#
--- a/usr/lib/node_modules/rednote-mcp/dist/tools/rednoteTools.js
+++ b/usr/lib/node_modules/rednote-mcp/dist/tools/rednoteTools.js
@@ -207,6 +207,21 @@
